fix: a sender that leaves a shared microphone becomes its own Me source

Two senders on one microphone formed one Me group. When one switched to
another microphone it kept the group, which recorded only the first
microphone, so the new one was never recorded. Senders still on their
group's microphone now claim it first; a sender that switched joins the
group already sending its new microphone, keeps its group when it is the
only sender, or else becomes a new Me source. The decision no longer
depends on sender order and holds across capture restarts.

